# ViewComponent's markup reaches the page through one class: Base, whose
# render entry dispatches the compiled template and returns the result
# (CWE-79). Component authors write the markup -- `call` methods and template
# files that interpolate request data, which is the documented way to author a
# component -- and Base decides whether that output is escaped on the way out.
# Before the fix, render_in returned the concatenation raw:
#
#   lib/view_component/base.rb
#     if render?
#       render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + output_postamble
#     else
#       ""
#     end
#
# so a component whose template interpolated a request value had that value
# inserted into the page unescaped. The fixing commit c43d8bafa7 (the 2.x
# backport) routes both halves through a shared helper that returns the text
# untouched when it is html_safe? and otherwise wraps it in html_escape:
#
#     def maybe_escape_html(text)
#       return text if request && !request.format.html?
#       return text if text.blank?
#       if text.html_safe?
#         text
#       else
#         yield
#         html_escape(text)
#       end
#     end
#
# Detected at class scope by
# vyql/bindings/ruby/component_base_template_render_without_escaping.vyql
# emitting code.UnescapedHtmlPresenter (VYQL-INJ-122): a Ruby class derived
# from ActionView::Base whose body dispatches render_template_for and carries
# no html_escape / escape_html / escapeHTML call. The class is the finest scope
# that holds both halves, because the escape ships as a helper on the same
# class rather than a call inside the render entry -- the entry's own call set
# cannot carry the discriminator, and the remediated base still dispatches the
# template renderer from the entry directly with the escape two helpers away
# (that shape is the fourth case below, and it rejects).
#
# Measured on the real checkout, three --cache off runs per revision (timeout
# 180, --max-ram 6GB): the parent of c43d8bafa7 reports one
# code.UnescapedHtmlPresenter flag at lib/view_component/base.rb:18 and one
# VYQL-INJ-122 row, against none on the fixed revision and none on the current
# default branch (whose base.rb calls render_template_for(...).to_s inside
# render_in itself and escapes in a sibling helper); every other row and flag
# is identical across all three trees apart from pure line shifts. Before the
# binding, both revisions reported the same 17 findings and 11 flags with
# nothing on the render pipeline -- the only HtmlRender sink is the unrelated
# render delegation at base.rb:202/207, which the fix does not touch.
#
# Precision. `render_template_for` occurs in no other clone in the corpus, and
# the only other `< ActionView::Base` subclass in any clone is a Redmine test
# helper with no template dispatch, which scans clean (3101 flags, none of
# them this concept). The escape conjunct is the vocabulary the Ruby
# core.HtmlEscape bindings already treat as an HTML escape, so a class that
# escapes through ERB::Util.html_escape, Rack::Utils.escape_html or
# CGI.escapeHTML is suppressed the same way as one escaping through the bare
# ActionView spelling.
#
# Residuals, all false-negative except the first: a class escaping only
# through ERB::Util's `h` alias or a `sanitize` call stays reported (`h` is too
# short a needle to key a negation on, and `sanitize` strips rather than
# escapes, with a name that collides with unrelated methods); the conjunct
# asks whether the class escapes anywhere rather than whether it escapes the
# render pipeline, so an escape in an unrelated method of the same class also
# suppresses; and the finding lands on the class declaration rather than the
# render method, because the render entry is not distinguishable at class
# scope. `html_safe` marks a string trusted without escaping it and is
# deliberately absent from the conjunct -- the remediated base uses it for the
# default postamble while the escape itself is html_escape, and a class that
# only marked strings trusted would still deserve the review (fifth case).
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed, case 1 expects and cases 2-5 reject.

test "rank1917: the component base returns template output and postamble unescaped"
  lang ruby
  file lib/view_component/base.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-122
  expect_review code.UnescapedHtmlPresenter
  code
  ```
  module ViewComponent
    class Base < ActionView::Base
      def render_in(view_context, &block)
        @view_context = view_context

        @lookup_context ||= view_context.lookup_context

        # For template variants (+phone, +desktop, etc.)
        @__vc_variant ||= @lookup_context.variants.first

        @__vc_render_in_block = block

        before_render

        if render?
          render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + output_postamble
        else
          ""
        end
      end

      # Optional content to be returned after the rendered template.
      #
      # @return [String]
      def output_postamble
        ""
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1917: the render entry routes template output through an escape helper"
  lang ruby
  file lib/view_component/base.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-122
  reject_review code.UnescapedHtmlPresenter
  code
  ```
  module ViewComponent
    class Base < ActionView::Base
      def render_in(view_context, &block)
        @view_context = view_context

        @lookup_context ||= view_context.lookup_context

        @__vc_variant ||= @lookup_context.variants.first

        @__vc_render_in_block = block

        before_render

        if render?
          # Avoid allocating new string when output_postamble is blank
          if output_postamble.blank?
            safe_render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s
          else
            safe_render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + safe_output_postamble
          end
        else
          ""
        end
      end

      def maybe_escape_html(text)
        return text if request && !request.format.html?
        return text if text.blank?

        if text.html_safe?
          text
        else
          yield
          html_escape(text)
        end
      end

      def safe_render_template_for(variant)
        if compiler.renders_template_for_variant?(variant)
          render_template_for(variant)
        else
          maybe_escape_html(render_template_for(variant)) do
            Kernel.warn("WARNING: The #{self.class} component rendered HTML-unsafe output. The output will be automatically escaped, but you may want to investigate.")
          end
        end
      end

      def safe_output_postamble
        maybe_escape_html(output_postamble) do
          Kernel.warn("WARNING: The #{self.class} component was provided an HTML-unsafe postamble. The postamble will be automatically escaped, but you may want to investigate.")
        end
      end

      def output_postamble
        @@default_output_postamble ||= "".html_safe
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1917: escaping through the CGI spelling suppresses the same way"
  lang ruby
  file lib/view_component/base.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-122
  reject_review code.UnescapedHtmlPresenter
  code
  ```
  module ViewComponent
    class Base < ActionView::Base
      def render_in(view_context, &block)
        @view_context = view_context

        before_render

        if render?
          safe_render_template_for(@__vc_variant).to_s + safe_output_postamble
        else
          ""
        end
      end

      def safe_render_template_for(variant)
        CGI.escapeHTML(render_template_for(variant))
      end

      def safe_output_postamble
        CGI.escapeHTML(output_postamble)
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1917: the base that dispatches the template from the entry itself but escapes in a helper rejects"
  lang ruby
  file lib/view_component/base.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-122
  reject_review code.UnescapedHtmlPresenter
  code
  ```
  module ViewComponent
    class Base < ActionView::Base
      def render_in(view_context, &block)
        @view_context = view_context

        before_render

        if render?
          inner = nil
          around_rendered = around_render do
            inner = render_template_for(@__vc_requested_details).to_s
          end

          rendered = if around_rendered.equal?(inner)
            around_rendered
          else
            __vc_safe_around_render_output(around_rendered)
          end

          if output_preamble.blank? && output_postamble.blank?
            rendered
          else
            __vc_safe_output_preamble + rendered + __vc_safe_output_postamble
          end
        else
          "".html_safe
        end
      end

      def __vc_maybe_escape_html(text)
        return text if request && !request.format.html?
        return text if text.blank?

        if text.html_safe?
          text
        else
          yield
          html_escape(text)
        end
      end

      def __vc_safe_output_postamble
        __vc_maybe_escape_html(output_postamble) do
          Kernel.warn("WARNING: The #{self.class} component was provided an HTML-unsafe postamble.")
        end
      end

      def __vc_safe_output_preamble
        __vc_maybe_escape_html(output_preamble) do
          Kernel.warn("WARNING: The #{self.class} component was provided an HTML-unsafe preamble.")
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

